WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
A chain drags a rollercoaster
slowly up the first hill.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.210
Then it lets go.

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.610
From that moment on,
there is no engine,

4
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.110
no motor and no more pushing.

5
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.590
The ride swoops down, races up
the next hill, dives again,

6
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.070
all on its own.

7
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.410
And on every ride like this,
that first hill is the tallest.

8
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:24.690
Why must the first hill be
the tallest on the ride?

9
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.470
In this mission, you'll see
that energy is never created or

10
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.180
destroyed.

11
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.590
You'll follow the energy as
the ride climbs and dives,

12
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.010
between gravitational
potential and kinetic energy,

13
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.930
and find out where some
of it goes along the way.

14
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.450
Your mission: explain why the
first hill must be the tallest.
